Lullaby from the Edge of Space and Time

Close your heavy eyes, traveler,
And let the atmosphere drift away.
The noise of the waking world has faded,
And the shadows of the conflict dissolve into grey.

Far beyond the rim of the solar winds,
Where ancient starlight begins to bend,
There is a quiet, velvet cradle waiting,
A timeless shore where all battles end.

Hush now, child of the stardust stream,
Float away on a cosmic dream.
Let the gravity of sorrow fall,
For the universe holds you, safe and small.

The nebulae are weaving a blanket of blue,
Spun from the silence of empty space.
No sirens echo through the quiet void,
Only the rhythm of a steady pulse and grace.

Lay down your armor of iron and tears,
Leave the history of the earth behind.
You are lighter than light-years away from fear,
In the infinite peace of the quiet mind.

Hush now, child of the stardust stream,
Float away on a cosmic dream.
The stars keep watch till the morning light,
Sleep, traveler. Rest tonight.

